Approach:

Typing  nc chatelaine.cylabacademy.net 32652 generates:
        We have identified a hash: 482c811da5d5b4bc6d497ffa98491e38
        Enter the password for identified hash: 
This is a md5 type of hash as it consists of 32 hexadecimal characters as md5 doesnt use automatic cryptographic salting
so reversing specific hash instantly maps back to the string password123.

next we are provided with:
        Flag is yet to be revealed!! Crack this hash: b7a875fc1ea228b9061041b7cec4bd3c52ab3ce3
        Enter the password for the identified hash:
Thos is a 40 hexadecimal character has which clarifies that it is SHA1 type of hash just like MD5 this hash also has common
dictionary phrases are highly vulnerable to precomputed lookup databases. the unencrpyted form was letmein.

the last has we got :
        Almost there!! Crack this hash: 916e8c4f79b25028c9e467f1eb8eee6d6bbdff965f9928310ad30a8d88697745
        Enter the password for the identified hash: 
This being a 64 hexa hash confirms to be sha256 which is mathematically stronger and more complex than the last 2 which on 
cracking gave the output as qwerty098 and thus we got our flag 

